        @* ================= CREATE RETURN ================= *@
        <section class="panel" id="panel-create-return" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-create-return" hidden>

            <header class="page-head">
                <div>
                    <h1 data-eyebrow="Mirakl &middot; Automation">Create Return</h1>
                    <p class="lede">
                        Files a return on the Mirakl back office for every row of the prepared list, by
                        driving a real browser window. Unlike the report modules this one
                        <strong>writes to the marketplace</strong> &mdash; each row it completes creates a
                        return that can only be undone by hand, so check the list before starting. Progress
                        streams in below as each order is processed.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <span class="stamp" id="cr-stamp"></span>
            </header>

            <div class="section-title">Mirakl session</div>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="session">
                    <span class="badge amber" id="cr-session-badge">Checking&hellip;</span>
                    <div class="actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="cr-login">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Open login window</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="cr-save-session" disabled>
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Save session</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="cr-clear-session">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Clear session</span>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="alert" id="cr-alert" role="alert">
                    <strong>Error</strong>
                    <span class="msg"></span>
                </div>

                <p class="note">
                    Mirakl signs in through Google SSO, which cannot be scripted. <strong>Open login
                    window</strong> launches Chrome on the order list &mdash; sign in there, then click
                    <strong>Save session</strong> and the cookies are encrypted to your Windows user account
                    and reused by every later run. Chrome is started on demand, so the first click takes a
                    few seconds.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="section-title">Prepare the list</div>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="uploader">
                    <div class="uploader-grid">
                        <label class="drop" id="cr-templateA-drop">
                            <span class="drop-step">Input 1</span>
                            <span class="drop-title">Return template A</span>
                            <span class="drop-hint">Marketplace Iade &amp; Degisim Talepleri</span>
                            <span class="drop-file"><span class="name"></span><span class="size"></span></span>
                            <input type="file" id="cr-templateA-file" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.csv"
                                   aria-label="Return template A file" />
                        </label>

                        <label class="drop" id="cr-templateB-drop">
                            <span class="drop-step">Input 2</span>
                            <span class="drop-title">Return template B</span>
                            <span class="drop-hint">The <code>&hellip;MP</code> file</span>
                            <span class="drop-file"><span class="name"></span><span class="size"></span></span>
                            <input type="file" id="cr-templateB-file" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.csv"
                                   aria-label="Return template B (MP) file" />
                        </label>

                        <label class="drop" id="cr-returns-drop">
                            <span class="drop-step">Input 3</span>
                            <span class="drop-title">Returns export</span>
                            <span class="drop-hint">Returns that already exist</span>
                            <span class="drop-file"><span class="name"></span><span class="size"></span></span>
                            <input type="file" id="cr-returns-file" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.csv"
                                   aria-label="Returns export file" />
                        </label>

                        <label class="drop" id="cr-orders-drop">
                            <span class="drop-step">Input 4</span>
                            <span class="drop-title">Orders export</span>
                            <span class="drop-hint">Supplies the full order number</span>
                            <span class="drop-file"><span class="name"></span><span class="size"></span></span>
                            <input type="file" id="cr-orders-file" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.csv"
                                   aria-label="Orders export file" />
                        </label>
                    </div>

                    <div class="filter-bar">
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="cr-from">Request date &mdash; from</label>
                            <input type="date" id="cr-from" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="cr-to">Request date &mdash; to</label>
                            <input type="date" id="cr-to" />
                        </div>
                        <label class="check" for="cr-returns-only">
                            <input type="checkbox" id="cr-returns-only" />
                            <span>Only &Idot;ade requests</span>
                        </label>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="cr-prepare">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Prepare list</span>
                        </button>
                    </div>

                    <div class="alert" id="cr-prepare-alert" role="alert">
                        <strong>Error</strong>
                        <span class="msg"></span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="note">
                    Both templates are filtered to rows that carry a real tracking code and fall inside the
                    date range, orders that appear twice are dropped entirely, and anything the returns
                    export already covers is left out. What survives is matched against the orders export to
                    get the full <code>01259_311911494-A</code> form the automation needs. A request the
                    marketplace has already <strong>cancelled</strong>, and an order the orders export reports
                    as <code>Canceled</code>, are both dropped there &mdash; neither can take a return, so
                    filing one would only cost a failed page. Nothing is uploaded anywhere and nothing is
                    stored &mdash; leaving this page discards it.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="skeleton" id="cr-prepare-skeleton">
                <partial name="_TowerLoader" model="TowerLoader.Automation()" />
            </div>

            <div class="results" id="cr-prepared" hidden>

                <div class="section-title">
                    How the list was narrowed down
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("cr-funnel-wrap", "Funnel", "Create Return")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Each step, and what survived it</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        The same sequence that used to be done by hand &mdash; read left to right, every drop
                        is the gap between two columns
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-scroll is-full" id="cr-funnel-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Ready to run
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("cr-ready-wrap", "Ready to run", "Create Return")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card accent-green">
                    <h3>Returns that will be filed</h3>
                    <p class="sub">One return per row &mdash; check this before starting, it cannot be undone from here</p>
                    <div class="table-scroll" id="cr-ready-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="cr-download">
                        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="btn-text">Download Excel</span>
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="cr-run-list">
                        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="btn-text">Start with this list</span>
                    </button>
                    <span class="filter-summary" id="cr-ready-summary"></span>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Left out
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("cr-excluded-wrap", "Left out", "Create Return")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card accent-amber">
                    <h3>Candidates that were dropped, and why</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        Only rows that got past the tracking-code and date filters appear here &mdash; those two
                        drop thousands of rows and are reported as counts in the table above instead
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-scroll" id="cr-excluded-wrap"></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="results" id="cr-run" hidden>
                <div class="section-title">Run log</div>
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="run-head">
                        <span>Orders processed</span>
                        <span class="mono" id="cr-progress-text">0 / 0</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="progress" id="cr-progress" role="progressbar"
                         aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="0"
                         aria-label="Create Return progress">
                        <span class="progress-fill" id="cr-progress-fill"></span>
                    </div>
                    <pre class="console" id="cr-console"></pre>
                </div>
                <p class="note">
                    An order that fails is screenshotted to <code>artifacts/create-return</code> beside the
                    executable and the run moves on to the next one &mdash; a batch is usually mostly good
                    rows, and the screenshot is what tells an expired session apart from a changed form.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="section-title">What gets filled in</div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Every return is filed the same way</h3>
                <p class="sub">
                    Only the order and its tracking number come from the list &mdash; the rest of the form is
                    fixed, and these are the values to change when the module is tailored further
                </p>
                <div class="table-scroll is-full">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Value</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>Quantity</td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Fixed</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Return method</td><td><code>By mail</code></td><td>Fixed</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Reason</td><td><code>Other reason</code></td><td>Fixed</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Carrier</td><td><code>Other</code></td><td>Fixed</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Name</td><td><code>Yurtici</code></td><td>Fixed</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Tracking number</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Prepared list</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Tracking address</td><td>Yurtiçi Kargo lookup URL</td><td>Built from the tracking number</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p class="note">
                    The form has no stable ids, so every field is found through its visible English label.
                    That is the part that breaks when Mirakl changes its UI &mdash; a failed run whose
                    screenshot shows a perfectly normal page usually means a label was renamed.
                </p>
            </div>

            <footer class="page-foot">Marketplace Reporting &middot; Create Return</footer>
