        @* ================= LATE ORDER WARNINGS ================= *@
        <section class="panel" id="panel-late-orders" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-late-orders" hidden>

            <header class="page-head">
                <div>
                    <h1 data-eyebrow="WhatsApp &middot; Automation">Late Order Warnings</h1>
                    <p class="lede">
                        Finds the orders that are <strong>overdue right now</strong> &mdash; not shipped, and past
                        their shipping deadline &mdash; groups them by seller, and composes one warning message per
                        seller for that seller's WhatsApp group. This is a different question from the Order
                        Report's late-shipment rate, which looks back at orders that <em>did</em> ship, late.
                        Messages to sellers cannot be recalled, so every one of them is shown in full below before
                        it goes anywhere.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <span class="stamp" id="lo-stamp"></span>
            </header>

            <div class="section-title">WhatsApp session</div>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="session">
                    <span class="badge amber" id="lo-session-badge">Checking&hellip;</span>
                    <div class="actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-login">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Open WhatsApp</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-check-session">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Check session</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-clear-session">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Clear session</span>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="alert" id="lo-session-alert" role="alert">
                    <strong>Error</strong>
                    <span class="msg"></span>
                </div>

                <p class="note">
                    <strong>Open WhatsApp</strong> launches a Chrome window on <code>web.whatsapp.com</code>. Scan
                    the QR code there once &mdash; there is deliberately <em>no</em> &ldquo;save session&rdquo;
                    button, because the profile keeps the login by itself and a button implying otherwise would be
                    a lie you would click and trust. Chrome starts on demand, so the first click takes a few
                    seconds.
                    <br /><br />
                    The profile lives at <code id="lo-profile-path"></code>. Unlike the Mirakl session this app
                    does not encrypt it &mdash; Chrome protects its own credential material against your Windows
                    account. Treat that folder as a credential: a live session can read and send in
                    <strong>every chat you are in</strong>, not only the seller groups.
                    <strong>Clear session</strong> deletes it and signs you out.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="section-title">Seller &rarr; WhatsApp group</div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Which group each seller gets messaged in</h3>
                <p class="sub">
                    Set this up once. The seller ID wins over the name when both are filled in &mdash; a seller can
                    rename their storefront, but their ID does not change
                </p>

                <div id="lo-mapping-warnings" hidden></div>

                <div class="table-scroll is-full">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th style="width: 16%">Seller ID</th>
                                <th style="width: 32%">Seller</th>
                                <th style="width: 42%">WhatsApp group</th>
                                <th style="width: 10%"></th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody id="lo-mapping-body"></tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-map-add">
                        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="btn-text">Add row</span>
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="lo-map-save">
                        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="btn-text">Save mapping</span>
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-map-import">
                        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="btn-text">Import from Excel</span>
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-map-export">
                        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="btn-text">Export to Excel</span>
                    </button>
                    <input type="file" id="lo-map-file" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.csv" hidden
                           aria-label="Seller/group mapping file" />
                    <span class="filter-summary" id="lo-mapping-count"></span>
                </div>

                <div class="alert" id="lo-mapping-alert" role="alert">
                    <strong>Error</strong>
                    <span class="msg"></span>
                </div>

                <p class="note">
                    The group name must match the WhatsApp group <strong>exactly</strong> &mdash; it is compared
                    character for character, and nothing is ever matched approximately. A near-match would post one
                    seller's order list into a different seller's group, which is why an ambiguous row is reported
                    rather than guessed at. A seller row with the group left blank counts as unmapped.
                    Stored at <code id="lo-mapping-path"></code> &mdash; <span id="lo-mapping-updated"></span>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="section-title">Find the overdue orders</div>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="uploader">
                    <div class="uploader-grid">
                        <label class="drop" id="lo-drop">
                            <span class="drop-step">Input</span>
                            <span class="drop-title">Orders export</span>
                            <span class="drop-hint">Mirakl orders export (.xlsx or .csv)</span>
                            <span class="drop-file"><span class="name"></span><span class="size"></span></span>
                            <input type="file" id="lo-file" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.csv"
                                   aria-label="Mirakl orders export" />
                        </label>
                    </div>

                    <div class="filter-bar">
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="lo-offset">Deadline offset (hours)</label>
                            <input type="number" id="lo-offset" step="0.5" value="0" />
                        </div>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="lo-prepare">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Find overdue orders</span>
                        </button>
                        <span class="filter-summary">Compared against <span id="lo-reference">now</span></span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="alert" id="lo-prepare-alert" role="alert">
                        <strong>Error</strong>
                        <span class="msg"></span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="note">
                    An order counts as overdue when its <code>Shipping date</code> is empty, its status is one the
                    seller can still act on (<code>Awaiting shipment</code> or <code>Pending acceptance</code>), and
                    its <code>Shipping deadline</code> has passed. Anything else is set aside for review rather than
                    messaged.
                    <br /><br />
                    <strong>About the offset:</strong> every deadline in the sample export lands at
                    <code>21:59:59</code>, which is <code>23:59:59</code> at UTC+2 &mdash; end of day in Berlin,
                    exported in UTC. If that holds, the offset for Turkish local time is <code>+3</code>. This field
                    is <em>temporary scaffolding</em>: open one overdue order in the Mirakl back office, compare the
                    deadline it shows against the file, set the offset to the difference, and once a second export
                    confirms it the value moves into the code and this field goes away. Nothing is uploaded anywhere
                    and nothing is stored &mdash; leaving this page discards it.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="skeleton" id="lo-prepare-skeleton">
                <partial name="_TowerLoader" model="TowerLoader.Automation()" />
            </div>

            <div class="results" id="lo-prepared" hidden>

                <div class="card accent-amber" id="lo-warnings" hidden>
                    <h3>Worth knowing about this file</h3>
                    <ul class="note-list" id="lo-warnings-list"></ul>
                </div>

                <div id="lo-unmapped" hidden>
                    <div class="section-title">
                        Sellers with no WhatsApp group
                        <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("lo-unmapped-wrap", "Unmapped sellers", "Late Orders")' />
                    </div>
                    <div class="card accent-amber">
                        <h3>These sellers are overdue and cannot be messaged</h3>
                        <p class="sub">
                            No message is composed for them and none is skipped silently &mdash; add the group above,
                            then run this again
                        </p>
                        <div class="table-scroll" id="lo-unmapped-wrap"></div>
                        <p class="note" id="lo-unmapped-summary"></p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Overdue orders
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("lo-orders-wrap", "Overdue orders", "Late Orders")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card accent-red">
                    <h3>Every order past its deadline and still unshipped</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        The exported deadline and the offset deadline sit side by side so the offset's effect is
                        visible on every row rather than taken on trust
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-scroll" id="lo-orders-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Where the rows went
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("lo-funnel-wrap", "Funnel", "Late Orders")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Every row in the file, accounted for</h3>
                    <p class="sub">The first six buckets are terminal and add up to the row count</p>
                    <div class="table-scroll is-full" id="lo-funnel-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Set aside for review
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("lo-review-wrap", "Set aside", "Late Orders")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card accent-amber">
                    <h3>Unshipped rows that were not turned into a warning</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        An unfamiliar status or an unreadable deadline lands here instead of defaulting into
                        &ldquo;chase the seller&rdquo;
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-scroll" id="lo-review-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">Message wording</div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>What each seller is sent</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        Two templates: the envelope is rendered once per seller, the order line once per overdue
                        order. Edits are saved with the mapping above
                    </p>

                    <div class="field">
                        <label for="lo-template">Message</label>
                        <textarea id="lo-template" rows="10" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
                    </div>
                    <div class="field" style="margin-top: 14px">
                        <label for="lo-line-template">Order line</label>
                        <textarea id="lo-line-template" rows="2" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
                    </div>

                    <p class="note">Placeholders: <span id="lo-placeholders"></span></p>

                    <div class="actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="lo-render">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Re-render messages</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-template-reset">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Reset to default</span>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">Messages</div>
                <div class="card accent-green">
                    <h3>One message per WhatsApp group, exactly as it will be sent</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        Read the group name on each card before you copy it &mdash; that is the last chance to catch
                        a wrong mapping. Seller accounts mapped to the same group are merged into one message, with
                        each account's orders listed under its own name
                    </p>

                    <div id="lo-messages"></div>

                    <div class="actions">
                        <label class="check" for="lo-dry-run">
                            <input type="checkbox" id="lo-dry-run" checked />
                            <span>Dry run (compose and verify, but do not send)</span>
                        </label>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="lo-send" disabled>
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Send messages</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-messages-export" disabled>
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Download messages (Excel)</span>
                        </button>
                        <span class="filter-summary" id="lo-messages-summary"></span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="alert" id="lo-messages-alert" role="alert">
                        <strong>Check this</strong>
                        <span class="msg"></span>
                    </div>

                    <p class="note">
                        A dry run opens every group, checks the title matches, types the message and reads it back
                        &mdash; then clears the box without sending. It exercises the whole path against real
                        production data with no outward effect, and it is the routine to run before every live send.
                        You can also still copy a message by hand from its card.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="results" id="lo-run" hidden>
                <div class="section-title">Run log</div>
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="run-head">
                        <span>Groups processed</span>
                        <span class="mono" id="lo-progress-text">0 / 0</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="progress" id="lo-progress" role="progressbar"
                         aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="0"
                         aria-label="Late Order Warnings progress">
                        <span class="progress-fill" id="lo-progress-fill"></span>
                    </div>
                    <pre class="console" id="lo-console"></pre>
                </div>
                <p class="note">
                    A group that fails is screenshotted to <code>artifacts/late-orders</code> beside the executable
                    and the run moves on. The one exception is a lost session: if WhatsApp drops back to the QR
                    code the whole run aborts, because every remaining group would fail identically.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="section-title">What happens when you send</div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>The sequence, per group</h3>
                <p class="sub">
                    Three checks stand between a mapping row and a message a seller can read &mdash; a WhatsApp
                    message cannot be recalled
                </p>
                <div class="table-scroll is-full">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>What it does</th><th>If it fails</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>Search</td><td>Clears the box, types the group name, waits for results to settle</td><td>Skips this seller</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Exact title match</strong></td><td>Matches the chat name character for character; requires exactly one hit</td><td>Skips &mdash; never picks one of two</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Header re-check</strong></td><td>Reads the opened chat's title back and compares again, after the click</td><td>Skips before typing anything</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Type</td><td>Whole lines at once, with Shift+Enter for the breaks (Enter would send)</td><td>Retypes key by key, then skips</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Read back</strong></td><td>Reads the composed text out of the box and compares it to what you approved</td><td>Clears the box, skips &mdash; names the differing line</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Send</td><td>Presses Enter, waits for the box to empty</td><td>Warns that it may have gone out</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Pause</td><td>6&ndash;12 s randomised on a live run; 0.7 s on a dry run, which sends nothing to pace</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p class="note">
                    At most <strong>40 groups per run</strong>; over that the run is refused rather than truncated.
                    Messages are capped at 4,000 characters. A run holds the app-wide automation slot for its whole
                    duration &mdash; roughly 5&ndash;8 minutes for a full batch &mdash; so Create Return cannot run
                    at the same time. The window stays visible on purpose: it is your only way to watch automation
                    touching your own WhatsApp account.
                </p>
            </div>

            <footer class="page-foot">Marketplace Reporting &middot; Late Order Warnings</footer>
        </section>

        @* ================= SELLER OFFER WARNINGS ================= *@
        <section class="panel" id="panel-offer-warnings" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-offer-warnings" hidden>

            <header class="page-head">
                <div>
                    <h1 data-eyebrow="Outlook &middot; Automation">Seller Offer Warnings</h1>
                </div>
                <span class="stamp" id="ow-stamp"></span>
            </header>

            <div class="section-title">Outlook</div>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="session">
                    <span class="badge amber" id="ow-outlook-badge">Not checked yet</span>
                    <div class="actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="ow-check-outlook">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Check Outlook</span>
                        </button>
